# Customer UI central theme

When designing or changing UI in `goldensoft-app` or `goldensoft-hr`:

## Source of truth

- Canonical tokens: `goldensoft-app/src/app/design-tokens.css`
- HR must keep an identical copy: `goldensoft-hr/src/app/design-tokens.css`
- After editing tokens in the app, run `npm run sync:design-tokens` in `goldensoft-hr`
- Contract: `goldensoft-app/docs/customer-ui-design-contract-v1.md`

## Do

- Use semantic tokens (`--color-*`, typography, space, radius, shadow)
- In HR, prefer `--hr-*` aliases under `.hr-root` that map to the contract
- Mobile-first; employee lists use circular `EmployeeAvatar`
- Thai dates: person+date cards use `formatThaiDateReadable` / `formatThaiDateRangeReadable`; forms use `ThaiDateInput`
- HR list/management screens follow `.cursor/rules/hr-list-surface-ux.mdc` (cards + FAB + overlay)
- Person + date cards follow `.cursor/rules/hr-person-date-cards.mdc` (leave/OT pattern, theme tokens only)

## Do not

- Import CSS from `goldensoft-platform`
- Invent a new purple/cream/AI-default palette
- Hardcode one-off brand colors when a token exists
- Add a second global header/sidebar inside HR when embedded in the customer shell
